    "html": "<p>Two containers X and Y are maintained at the same temperature. X has volume <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4 m^{3}\"></span> and Y has volume <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6 m^{3}\"></span>. They both hold an ideal gas. The pressure in X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100 Pa\"></span> and the pressure in Y is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50 Pa\"></span>. The containers are then joined by a tube of negligible volume. What is the final pressure in the containers?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"70 Pa\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"75 Pa\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"80 Pa\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"150 Pa\"></span></li></ol>"
